markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Copying Data: Undo & Reset

Sometimes your app should filter or transform data without permanently changing it.
Other times, data will change and users need a way to recover when they make a mistake.

## When should we copy data?

Copy data when you want to try something (like filtering, sorting, or editing) without losing the original.

**This is especially important when:**

- Users might want to undo an action

- Users might want to reset back to the original state

- Multiple parts of your app rely on the same dataset

<div style="background-color:#e4e2f8; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; margin:18px auto; max-width:85%;"> <p style="font-size:12pt; margin:0; line-height:135%;"><strong>Key idea:</strong> If you mutate the original data, you can’t easily “go back” unless you saved a copy first.</p> </div>

<iframe src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit4_testing/undo_reset_flip_cards.html" width="100%" height="290" style="border:none;" title="Undo vs Reset flip cards"></iframe>

---



<img src="https://images.code.org/8fcfacdaf4be65223e4409f847e0df09-image-1769615559049.png" alt="spreadsheet with the drop down showing undo and redo" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 20px 00px 20px;">

## Real-world examples: Undo and Reset

Think about tools like word processors, drawing apps, or photo editors.

**They work because they support recovery:**

- Undo lets you step back one change at a time

- Reset restores the original version all at once

Users expect these options because mistakes are normal. A good interface helps them recover quickly.

<div style="clear:both;"></div>


## Reflect

**Take a moment to reflect before moving on**.

- What do undo and reset help you do as a user?

- What information would an app need to store to make undo/reset possible?

- How could changing the original data make recovery harder?

<details style="background-color:#ececec;padding:12px;margin-bottom:10px;border:1px solid #D9E3E5;border-radius:8px;box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
  <summary style="font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold;">💡 Check your thinking</summary> <div style="margin-top:12px; margin-left:14px; margin-right:14px; margin-bottom:10px; font-size:13pt; line-height:145%;"> <ul> <li style = "font-size: 12pt";>Undo and reset let users recover from mistakes without fear. They support experimentation by making it safe to try things and go back if something doesn’t work.</li> <li style = "font-size: 12pt">The app needs access to a previous version of the data (often the original state or a history of changes) so it can restore what existed before the change.</li> <li style = "font-size: 12pt">If the original data is mutated, the previous state is lost. Without a saved copy, the app has nothing to return to, making undo or reset difficult or impossible.</li> </ul> </div> </details>







